markucz@gmail.com wrote:
> What's the prob: I found a bookshop (a pretty big one) and naturally I
> want to, er, borrow some books and scrolls. I have 3 tripe rations and
> a whistle. Do you think there will be any effect if I give a ration to
> the dog each time it drops something and blow the whistle immediately
> after that? The idea behind this Pavlov experiment is to train the dog
> to steal stuff so that eventually I won't have to give it any food. (As
> I said, I only have 3 tripe rations and nothing else a dog would eat.)
> Has anybody tried to do something like this?

Tame dogs and cats can be trained; this is well known. Whistles have
nothing to do with it though.  Stand on the entrance square to the shop
(right where the door is).  Wait for your pet to drop an item right on
the free square immediately inside the shop -- not the squares
diagonally adjacent, just the one where you can pick it up for free.
When your pet drops something there, throw him a tripe ration within
about 4 turns.  It must be a tripe ration, and it must be soon after he
drops it.  Once this is done, your pet is trained and will fetch
everything it can from the shop and drop it for you.  (It will try to
avoid stepping on squares with cursed items, so it will probably not
get items from a pile including a cursed item). The training wears off
after a while but can be redone.



